      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6b8f8227a56787575ebc0|full_name}: Yup, this is the process that I use. I either do it on the loading screen when the Go button appears, or I open up one of the menus and switch windows then. When the cursor isn't locked (in a menu), you are able to move the cursor out and select another window. It's honestly not that hard to do and can be done rather quickly.\n\nI would prefer to keep the mouse locked sometimes because on the rare occasion that my controllers are dead or I'm testing something, I'd like to still play with my headset on and with the keyboard and mouse. If the mouse is never locked in VR mode, then I would not be able to play in VR with the hybrid setup.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
